   "text": "http : / / www . citypress . co . za / news / france - hit - another - jewellery - heist / France <8 hit> by another jewellery <9 heist> 9 September 2013 11 : 55 Four men <10 rammed> their car into an up - market jewellery store in central Paris today , <11 smashing> the shop window and <12 making off> with a €2 million ( R26 million ) booty , a police source <15 said> . The <13 heist> near the upscale Place Vendome is the latest to <14 hit> France after a <2 spate> of high - profile <3 robberies> in the southern resort of Cannes . The police source , who <4 wished> to <1 remain> <17 anonymous> , <16 said> the men <5 drove> a large 4×4 car into the store in the early hours of the morning , and <6 grabbed> jewellery and luxury watches <18 worth> an <7 estimated> €2 million . They then set fire to the vehicle and escaped in another car . Forensic policemen are currently going through the site of the robbery at the Casty store on Rue de Castiglione in the central first district of Paris , which is home to numerous jewellery shops . At the end of July , an armed man carried out a brazen robbery in broad daylight at a diamond exhibition at the Carlton hotel in Cannes , making off with jewellery worth €103 million in one of the world ’ s biggest heists . Paris has also been the scene of high - profile robberies . In December 2008 , three men emptied almost all of the stock of gems from the Harry Winston jewellery store . In 2009 , police said they had recovered 80% of the haul .",
